  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Three zones – get goal side",
  "description": "Use the rink's three zones. In each zone there is one attacker (blue) and one defender (red). Two attackers with a puck start at the goal line and skate into the first zone, making it 3 v 1.\n\nThe attackers must get through all three zones. When they cross a line into the next zone, everyone – attackers and defenders – may follow. So the defender who has been beaten must skate back quickly and get goal side in the next zone, making the overload smaller. Finish with a shot on goal in the last zone.\n\nIf the defenders win the puck they score by playing it over the goal line where the attackers started. Swap roles after a while. For younger players, one zone can be split into three smaller zones with cones.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Defender: if you are beaten – skate back the shortest way towards the net, not towards the puck."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Get between the puck and the net before you try to win the puck."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Steer the puck carrier towards the boards, away from the middle."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Attackers: use the overload quickly, before the defenders get back."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 3,
